# GitHub sync

Remote: https://github.com/SNDP-Design/XWriter.git
Branch: `main`

Whenever a request changes files in this project, commit those changes and push them to that repository before the task is finished.

- Stage the project files for the change. Do not commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, tokens).
- Write a 1–2 sentence commit message that says why the change was made.
- Push to `origin` on `main`. Do not force-push.
- Do not change git config, skip hooks, or amend a commit that has already been pushed.
- If GitHub login or the push fails, say so. Do not claim the push succeeded.

```bash
git add -A
git commit -m "Explain why this change was made."
git push origin main
```
